## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical E2E testing skills around feature flags, data seeding, cross-device validation, and deterministic mocks. It also evaluates how candidates handle paralellization, event deduplication, and rollback correctness in a live-like rollout.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and gradual rollouts
- Deterministic data seeding for stable tests
- Mocking external services (flag service, analytics)
- Cross-device (desktop/mobile) parity and isolation
- Event deduplication and correct rollback behavior

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton for ranking_v2 on/off
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('ranking_v2 enabled shows new ranking and analytics', async ({ page, request }) => {
  // seed data and mock flag service to return true for ranking_v2
  // navigate to search and verify ordering matches ranking_v2
  // assert analytics endpoint received a single event per click
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate rollout skew and handle hotfix rollbacks?
- How would you scale this test to 1000+ products with performance constraints?

